      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(runway): apply configured request policy to video generation requests",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nRunway video generation currently ignores `models.providers.runway.request` overrides (headers, allowPrivateNetwork, dispatcherPolicy). Users who configure a request policy for Runway see it applied to chat/completion providers but not to video generation, so private-network access, custom headers, and dispatcher routing are dropped on the floor.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nMirror the pattern already used by `openai`, `pixverse`, `google` image generation, and Alix-007's recent DashScope/MiniMax/OpenRouter video request-policy PRs: pass `sanitizeConfiguredModelProviderRequest(providerConfig?.request)` into `resolveProviderHttpRequestConfig` so the configured transport overrides flow into the create request.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `extensions/runway/video-generation-provider.ts`\n  - Import `sanitizeConfiguredModelProviderRequest`.\n  - Read `req.cfg?.models?.providers?.runway`.\n  - Forward the sanitized request policy to `resolveProviderHttpRequestConfig`.\n- `extensions/runway/video-generation-provider.test.ts`\n  - Add regression test asserting that configured headers, `allowPrivateNetwork`, and `dispatcherPolicy` reach `postJsonRequest`.\n  - Fix test type errors caught by `check-test-types`.\n\n## Intentionally Out of Scope\n\n- Poll/download stages continue to use the headers resolved at create time; this change does not refactor them onto `fetchWithTimeoutGuarded`, matching the minimal scope of the existing video request-policy PRs.\n- No new helper or shared abstraction is introduced.\n\n## Evidence\n\n```bash\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/runway/video-generation-provider.test.ts\nnode scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -p test/tsconfig/tsconfig.extensions.test.json --incremental --tsBuildInfoFile .artifacts/tsgo-cache/extensions-test.tsbuildinfo\nnode scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -p tsconfig.extensions.json --incremental --tsBuildInfoFile .artifacts/tsgo-cache/extensions.tsbuildinfo\nnode scripts/run-oxlint.mjs --tsconfig config/tsconfig/oxlint.extensions.json extensions/runway/video-generation-provider.ts extensions/runway/video-generation-provider.test.ts\n```\n\n- Vitest: 10/10 passing.\n- `tsgo` (source + test): no type errors.\n- `oxlint`: clean.\n\nReal behavior proof against a local Runway-compatible endpoint, showing the configured `X-Runway-Policy` header is sent and private-network access is allowed:\n\n```\n[proof] local Runway-compatible endpoint at http://127.0.0.1:37479\n[server] POST /v1/text_to_video\n[server] Authorization: Bearer dummy-runway-key\n[server] X-Runway-Policy: runway-policy\n[server] GET /v1/tasks/task-proof\n[server] GET /video.mp4\n[proof] generated video count: 1\n[proof] video MIME type: video/mp4\n[proof] done\n```\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
        "branch": "cz/runway-video-request-policy",
